## Context and author decisions

Brood is explicitly requested post-Dream crystallisation, separate from Roar
(factual capture) and Dream (memory consolidation). The 2026-10-05 author
replaces this ticket's original pre-planning incubation and retrospective audit.
That historical rationale remains in Git history; generic exploration remains
valuable in raid Imagine and is not a prerequisite or deliverable here.

A project Brood opens a local ticket and implementation merge request. When it
nominates a harness change, its local implementation is the proof of concept;
it files only a detailed nomination ticket in the explicitly named harness.
The harness implementor examines nominations across projects, judges whether
they work, generalizes and validates. Brood implementors may annotate, simplify
and decay consolidated memory; source experiences remain append-only.

## Actions

- Implement a minimal explicit-invocation `skills/brood/SKILL.md`; distinguish
  project implementation from harness nomination and harness implementation.
- Reconcile the live v8 design §7, delivery plan, governance instructions and
  templates, and deferred 0925 without changing Roar/Dream's authority.
- Define when promotion is justified: benefit evidence versus feasibility,
  context and maintenance cost, exceptions, counterexamples and provenance;
  shared-origin or copied nominations are not independent confirmations.
- Examine accepted Dream revisions plus preserved source experiences and
  unresolved conflicts. Current rule authority is not proof of effectiveness;
  Brood may simplify/remove bad rules as well as introduce improvements.
- Preserve proposal/implementation/validation distinctions; memory decay needs
  replacement evidence, preserved sources and counterexamples. Recheck source
  revisions before writing; reconcile concurrent Dream changes.
- Require audience clearance or a sanitized reproducer for nominations. After
  harness adoption link back to local implementations for replacement or a
  justified retained exception; avoid duplicate drift.

## Relevant files

`skills/dream/SKILL.md`, `memory/DREAM.md`, `AGENTS.md`,
`docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`,
`docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`, `docs/memory-v8/templates/`,
`tickets/0925-deferred-crystallisation-only-on-explici.erg`,
`memory/topics/memory-v8-governance.md`, `README.md`.

## Test and verification

Exercise the skill in isolated synthetic project/harness fixtures: local
improvement and harness nomination; cross-project evidence including copied
origins; rule counterexample/no-change; incomplete evidence/privacy and changed
Dream revisions. Inspect observable outputs, destination boundaries and source
preservation; wording-only assertions do not establish skill behavior.
Regenerate the catalog and run meaningful checks. Record review limitations
honestly; no manufactured historical evidence or implied automatic promotion.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Minimal Brood implements the author-approved project/harness workflow,
      evidence-led promotion timing and allowed consolidated-memory edits.
- [ ] Live design/governance/templates and deferred 0925 consistently distinguish
      explicit Brood nominations from forbidden Roar/Dream promotions.
- [ ] Behavior evaluation demonstrates destination boundaries, evidence limits,
      source preservation, revision coordination and adoption return path.
- [ ] Independent review findings are resolved; catalog is current and `make check`
      and `tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
